<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-code-traceability-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Code-to-model traceability: 55/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The CA section is well traced: every function docstring states the equation it implements and the source (Rule 30 Boolean/ANF, Jen 1990 inverse, diagonal recursion, Boolean Jacobian, prize problems 1-3), and the figure text repeats the identities. The PDE section cites Meinhardt-Klingler 1987 Eq. 5 and Meinhardt 1995 Ch. 5-6 but the implemented equations, variable roles (b as a relaxation divisor) and parameter symbols (rho, rho0, kappa, mu_a, sigma_s, mu_s, mu_b) do not correspond to those sources, and the stochastic injection and clipping steps have no citation at all (deduction 20). The Raup mesh names W, D, T, S but the envelope constants and the T*rc translation have no equation or figure reference (deduction 10). The lesion experiment cites M&K 1987 Fig. 12, but the cell-sorting and bioelectric panels cite papers by name only and hard-code the 0.583 threshold and a 0.36 factor that the labels call 0.40 (deduction 10). Two figure labels are hard-coded strings rather than computed values (deduction 5)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-code-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-code-traceability-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-model-fidelity-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Model fidelity to source: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "I verified by hand that the Boolean form l XOR (c OR r) and the GF(2) ANF reproduce the Rule 30 truth table (00011110), that run_eca uses the standard Wolfram neighbourhood indexing so Rule 90 is also correct, that Jen's inverse a_{t,i-1} = a_{t+1,i} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1}) follows algebraically and is applied with the right time offsets, that the diagonal recursion d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) XOR (d_{k-1}(t) OR d_k(t)) is an exact change of variables, and that the three Boolean partial derivatives are right; the CA half is exemplary. The Meinhardt-Klingler half is a loose analogue, not the published equations: autocatalysis is divided by a relaxation variable b with db/dt = mu_b (a - b), which is neither the 1987 activator-depleted-substrate system nor the hormone that modulates activator decay in the Oliva model, parameter names and values are unsourced, and a stochastic rule injecting +0.90 activator at random high-substrate sites plus hard clipping of a, s, b is load-bearing (with the injection removed the pattern extinguishes to 0.9 percent pigment in steps 148-221 and a saturates at the 5.0 clip); deduction 20. The Raup mesh uses W^(theta/2pi) and r_c = a(1+D)/(1-D) correctly but replaces Raup's generating curve with an ad hoc envelope carrying six unsourced constants, so that T has no effect on the silhouette for T in [0, 0.36]; deduction 10. Remaining 8 points lost for over-naming a sufficiency check as an iff theorem, a 0.36 vs 0.40 D2 mismatch in the bioelectric panel, and cross-model panels that are toy re-implementations." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-morphometric-validation-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Morphometric validation: 45/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Quantitative metrics are genuinely computed on the output and compared to specimen numbers: H/W 1.8342 vs 1.8330, silhouette IoU 0.835, white-chord mean/CV, KS of mean-normalised chords, pigment fraction and a box-counting dimension, all written to CSV and drawn in panel F; the Rule 30 geometric law P(W=w)=2^-w (mean 2, CV 0.707) is correctly derived and confirmed. Deductions: the chord metric has no discriminating power, since Rule 90 (KS 0.2627, CV 0.697) and Rule 150 (KS 0.252) match Rule 30 (KS 0.2623, CV 0.7075) and Rule 110 scores better (KS 0.2448), and the specimen CV 0.640 is actually closer to the Rule 90 control; this is never stated (deduction 20). The box-counting estimator returns 2.155 for iid random bits and 2.17 for Rule 30, which is impossible for a planar set, so D_box is invalid (deduction 10). H/W and IoU are calibration, not validation: the mesh constants were tuned to the same single outline the self-test then asserts within 1.5 percent (deduction 10). The specimen-derived numbers are not reproducible (no segmentation code; the 1814 chord runs cannot be regenerated from the vendored 148x92 lattice, which yields 667 runs of mean 11.5), only one of two specimens is used quantitatively, and the Meinhardt CV test window 0.60-1.35 is nearly vacuous (deduction 15)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-measurement-2d-shell-silhouette-iou-vs-segmented-conus-textile-specimen>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-measurement-3d-raup-conus-textile-shell-height-to-width-ratio-h-w>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-measurement-jen-1990-left-bijective-inverse-diagonal-recursion-bit-errors>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-measurement-left-cone-periodic-crystal-lock-in-front-velocity-v-lock>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-measurement-rule-30-center-column-exact-match-to-oeis-a051023-first-128-bits>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-measurement-rule-30-prize-2-center-column-density-c-1024>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-measurement-rule-30-white-tent-chord-length-cv>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-morphometric-validation-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-morphometric-validation-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-overall-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — MorphoEval overall 50.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Blinded second-assessor pass. The script evolves Wolfram's elementary CA Rule 30 (plus a Rule 90 control) on a periodic ring, verifies the centre column against OEIS A051023, checks Jen's left-bijective inverse, the left-cone diagonal recursion and period-doubling lock-in cascade, and a Boolean-Jacobian damage cone. In parallel it integrates a three-variable activator/substrate/relaxation PDE labelled Meinhardt-Klingler (1987) with an added stochastic activator-injection rule, texture-maps both space-time sheets onto a single fixed Raup-style biconical mesh, and compares silhouette H/W, IoU, white-chord statistics and a box-counting dimension against numbers vendored in a SHA-256-pinned fixture derived (by unpublished means) from two Wikimedia Conus textile photographs. A second figure adds unrelated cell-sorting and bioelectric domain-wall kymographs. I re-ran the script (35 s) and obtained byte-identical CSV, PNG and GIF outputs. Overall 50.5/100 (faithfulness 42.4, reproducibility 69.2; model-implementation 47.3/100, biological-validation 38.8/100, applicable-only overall 50.5/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit fb234bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 62, Morphological realism / specimen match 35, Parameter expressivity 18, Morphometric validation 45, Source and data traceability 70, Code-to-model traceability 55, Reproducibility package 78. Output judged: conus_textile_rule30_comparison.png: rendered output of 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py at fb234bc, image/png, 611089 B, 2640×1632 px, artifact_sha256 b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41 (sha256 b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41), spec_fingerprint 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313; artifact_sha256: b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/conus/conus_textile_reference.json=dfcb500d87a39390...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Bioelectric panel inconsistency: D2_blocked = 0.36*D1 at 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py:595 while the CSV governing_law string (line 1272) and panel F x-label (line 1495) state 0.40; panel D label at line 1426 hard-codes 'v_L=-0.26' instead of the measured value.",
        "remediation needed: DOI disagreement for Wolfram 1986 (10.1016/0196-8858(86)90029-1 at 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py:11 and datasets/conus/paper_citations.bib:20 vs 90028-X in README) and for Meinhardt 1995 (978-3-662-03125-4 at line 19 and bib line 61 vs 03107-0 in README); at least one of each pair is wrong.",
        "remediation needed: DOI resolution by the audit integrator (Crossref, 2026-10-19), not part of the blinded pass: Wolfram 1986 is 10.1016/0196-8858(86)90028-X (the README is right; script line 11 and paper_citations.bib line 20 carry the DOI of an unrelated Adv. Appl. Math. paper), and Meinhardt 1995 is 10.1007/978-3-662-13135-0 (neither 978-3-662-03107-0 in the README nor 978-3-662-03125-4 in the script and .bib is the book; they resolve to unrelated Springer volumes).",
        "remediation needed: Fixture provenance is broken: stjohn_white_chord_runs_px (1814 runs, mean 26.9 px) cannot be regenerated from body_whorl_tents_148x92_bitstrings (667 runs, mean 11.5) and no segmentation script exists in the worktree; unpack_specimen_masks at 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py:125-134 simply trusts the vendored arrays.",
        "remediation needed: README-documented flags --no-photos and --no-anim are not implemented; argparse at 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py:1507-1514 rejects them with exit code 2, and --self-test only works via prefix abbreviation of --self-test-only.",
        "remediation needed: Raup translation parameter T is inert in the range used: raup_conus_mesh (1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py:688-703) gives identical H/W 1.8342 for T=0.0 and T=0.36 because Z extent is set by the ad hoc axial_ext constants at line 699 times S; W, D, T, S are never swept.",
        "remediation needed: The 'Meinhardt-Klingler' PDE at 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py:645-660 adds an unsourced stochastic activator injection (p=0.18 per substep, +0.90 at a random high-substrate site) and hard clipping; with the injection removed the pattern extinguishes (0.9 percent pigment over steps 148-221) and activator saturates at the 5.0 clip, so the published equations alone do not produce the shown output.",
        "remediation needed: The white-chord morphometric cannot discriminate the hypothesis from controls: with the same seed/grid, Rule 90 gives KS 0.2627 and Rule 150 KS 0.252 vs Rule 30 KS 0.2623, and Rule 110 does better (KS 0.2448); self_test lines 844-850 and write_metrics_csv lines 919-970 never flag this.",
        "remediation needed: box_counting_dimension (1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py:740-753) returns 2.155 for iid random bits and 2.17 for Rule 30, exceeding the planar bound of 2, so the D_box column in conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv is an estimator artefact of the 2..32 scale range on a 148x92 grid." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.05e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-parameter-expressivity-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Parameter expressivity: 18/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "No morphospace parameter is swept or exposed. raup_conus_mesh is called once with the defaults W=1.28, D=0.42, T=0.36, S=5.99 and the PDE constants are hard-coded inside run_meinhardt_conus; the only CLI knobs are --frames and --fps. I probed the mesh myself: W 1.28 to 1.5 moves H/W 1.834 to 1.912 and S 5.99 to 3.0 moves it to 0.919, so W, D and S do act, but T=0.0 and T=0.36 yield identical H/W 1.8342 and IoU within 0.0005, meaning the translation parameter does not control spire height in the range used (deduction 25). The absence of any sweep, montage or figure demonstrating monotonic control of form costs a further 45; the Rule 90 control and the seed/k scans in the defect-front figure are diagnostics, not morphospace exploration, and earn only partial credit. Twelve further points are withheld because the PDE regime cannot be varied without editing source." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-parameter-expressivity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 1.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "not faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-repro-package-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Reproducibility package: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "requirements.txt gives lower bounds and requirements.lock.txt gives exact pins with Python 3.14.7, platform and date; every RNG is seeded (42, 17, 100+idx) and no wall clock or unseeded randomness is used. I re-ran the script from the worktree in about 35 s and all five artefacts (two CSVs, two PNGs, GIF) were byte-identical to the shipped ones, which is the strongest possible determinism evidence. The fixture is verified at load and the run works offline. Deductions: the README's documented invocation is wrong, since --no-photos and --no-anim do not exist (argparse exits 2) and --self-test only works through argparse prefix abbreviation of --self-test-only (deduction 12). There is no regeneration path for the specimen-derived fixture, so the input side of the package is not reproducible (deduction 6). No test runner or CI hook wraps the self-test, and matplotlib emits cache-directory warnings when HOME is not writable (deduction 4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-repro-package-3>,
