<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-source-traceability-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Source and data traceability: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "All seven primary papers carry journal, volume, pages and DOI in both the module docstring and datasets/conus/paper_citations.bib, and the Rule 30 prize URL and OEIS id are given. Input provenance is strong where it exists: the fixture JSON is SHA-256 pinned and verified on every run, both photographs have Wikimedia URL, author, licence, byte count and SHA-256 which are checked on --download, and I confirmed all three digests match the files on disk. Deductions: the specimen-derived content of the fixture (silhouette row bounds, 148x92 tent lattice, 1814 chord runs) has no generating code or method description anywhere in the worktree, so the chain from photograph to number is broken and the lattice and chord list are mutually inconsistent (deduction 15). The Wolfram 1986 DOI in the script and bib (…90029-1) differs from the one in the README (…90028-X), and the Meinhardt 1995 DOI likewise (…03125-4 vs …03107-0); at least one of each pair is wrong and I could not resolve them from the sandbox (deduction 8). Zhang 2025, Cervera 2021 and the PlanformDB threshold 0.583 are invoked in code without any identifier in this script or fixture (deduction 7)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-source-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-source-traceability-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-specimen-match-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 35/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "I viewed both cached photographs and all rendered outputs side by side. Real Conus textile shows thin dark reticulated lines bounding large white tents at fine scale over a smooth cone; the rendered Rule 30 kymograph (random initial row, 50 percent density, one cell = 2 px) reads as binary noise, and the 3D Rule 30 shell carries a 90x54 block texture that looks like a checkerboard rather than tents; the Meinhardt kymograph shows a few horizontal bands and sparse V shapes on blank cream and the Meinhardt shell is almost uniformly cream in both the PNG and GIF. Pigment fraction 0.50 (Rule 30) vs 0.355 (specimen) is tabulated but never addressed. Credit is given for the shell outline: the biconical mesh is recognisably a cone shell and its silhouette IoU of 0.835 against the fixture outline is a genuine quantitative overlap (deduction 10 for a visibly wider shoulder and spire than the specimen in panel C). The photographs themselves are only hashed, never displayed or analysed, so no figure places the model next to a real specimen (deduction 20); pigment-pattern realism is poor at the rendered resolution (deduction 35). Rule 30 and the Meinhardt output are visually distinct from each other, which is the one criterion fully met." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 3.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

